# plists.defer -- launchd units staged behind an explicit gate (DGN-227 E1-1).
# One plist basename per line; '#' comments allowed. Loaders (install.sh
# schedule_routines_launchd + mint_run.sh start) SKIP these on the default
# scan; they load only via an explicit `mint_run.sh start --deferred` call
# (domain install path / C2 swap / E3 resolution / G3 alignment).
# NOTE: mint.sh renders 'telegram-agent' to the minted agent name in this
# file (same substitution as the plist filenames).
#
# DGN-1286 item 2b: the three generic-brief units below are NO LONGER shipped
# by agents/.template/routines -- they moved to kit-handover/kit_life/payload/
# routines/ on their way to the dogany-lifekit payload (a kitless base-kit
# agent should not own a morning brief / daily retro / weekly retro). The
# entries STAY here on purpose. This file is a basename deny-list, not an
# inventory: an entry naming a file that is not present is inert, and keeping
# the names means that when a kit later drops those units into an instance's
# routines/ they are STILL deferred rather than silently auto-loaded by the
# next default scan. Removing the lines would delete the deferral policy
# together with the files and hand the kit an auto-loading briefing set.
# The framework keeps the briefing machinery either way: generic-brief.sh,
# lib/brief-slot-ctl.sh, set-briefing-times.sh.
com.telegram-skill-bot.telegram-agent.generic-brief-morning.plist
com.telegram-skill-bot.telegram-agent.generic-brief-retro.plist
com.telegram-skill-bot.telegram-agent.generic-brief-weekly.plist
